  "configuration_id": "config_017",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) achieved 52.66% acc / 51.04% F1, outperforming RNA alone (config_001: 48.49%) by ~4.2 points, confirming that the weak image modality (config_010: 20.79%) still adds complementary signal. However, we have only tested one fusion strategy (concat). Question: Does weighted fusion outperform simple concatenation for combining the asymmetrically-contributing RNA and image representations? config_017 is identical to config_016 except fusion changes from concat to weighted, making this a clean single-variable A/B test. Why this is the best next experiment: it directly extends our strongest configuration, isolates exactly one design decision (fusion method), and the answer will inform the fusion choice for all subsequent multimodal experiments (multiprofile, alternative encoders). Under a limited budget, resolving whether fusion strategy matters before scaling to more complex settings (multiprofile, transformer aggregation, different encoders) avoids wasting experiments on a suboptimal fusion baseline."
}

